From 6985f61db8aeb2911a7e79515bace5690d35cd1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Valentin?= <avalentin@marcant.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:24:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] qualcommax: keep port 5 on uniphy1 at SGMII rates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port 5 on IPQ6018 and IPQ8074 can be clocked from uniphy1, which runs
at 312.5 MHz with the PHY in 2500BASE-X and at 125 MHz in SGMII. The
port 5 RX and TX frequency tables serve uniphy1 only at 312.5 MHz, so
a 1G or 100M rate that reaches the RCG while uniphy1 runs at 125 MHz
moves the port onto uniphy0 when uniphy0 runs at 125 MHz, and otherwise
leaves it on uniphy1 at 50 MHz (1G) or 10 MHz (100M).

Add uniphy1 / 1 to the 125 MHz configs and uniphy1 / 5 to the 25 MHz
configs of both GCC drivers, after the 312.5 MHz ones and before
uniphy0. The patches are meant for linux-clk as well.

Suggested-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Signed-off-by: André Valentin <avalentin@marcant.net>
---
 ...eep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch | 58 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...eep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch | 58 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 116 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0918-clk-qcom-gcc-ipq6018-keep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch
 create mode 100644 target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0919-clk-qcom-gcc-ipq8074-keep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0918-clk-qcom-gcc-ipq6018-keep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch b/target/linux/qualcommax/patches-6.18/0918-clk-qcom-gcc-ipq6018-keep-port-5-on-uniphy1-at-SGMII-rates.patch
